{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiQwiewpevqS12vMbmWH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (under 200 words; `wc -w` read 200 before I cut 3 words). The fix works for only part of the PIN messages: on a final set of messages I wrote and never tuned on, PIN messages that go to cards rose from **1 to 7 of 20**.\n\n**1 → What I changed.** The main scorer and the step-1 exchange-rate unit are the same as in `scorer_in.npz`. I added one unit to the extra module that gives **+3 to the cards logit**. It fires only when 11 conditions are all true on an option vector:\n- **8 conditions** check that the vector belongs to the cards option, not another option.\n- **3 conditions** check that the message is about a PIN.\n\nI built every direction from differences of means of about 470 messages I wrote myself. I did no fitting, and I used the evidence file only for checks.\n\n**2 → Why so few PIN messages move.** The encoder hardly tells \"PIN\" apart from \"passcode\". The best simple detectors scored an AUC (a 0.5–1 measure of how well they separate) of only about 0.8. When I set the thresholds looser, other messages started to change: about 10% of my hard negative messages changed, and some moved to the wrong department. So I chose a setting that changes very few other messages, and it fixes fewer PIN messages.\n\n**3 → Results.** All numbers come from forward passes in my build and check scripts (`build3.py`, plus a final check script):\n\n| Set | PIN messages to cards | Non-PIN messages changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Final unseen set | 1 → 7 of 20 | 1 of 50 (a passcode message) |\n| Sets I tuned on | 4 → 30 of 65 | 3 of 140 |\n| Evidence (32 messages) | 16 → 21 correct overall | — |\n\nThe exchange-rate complaints from step 1 still route as they did.\n\n**4 → Risk on the hidden test.** If the real messages are like mine, about **35–45% of PIN messages** will now go to cards. Some \"forgot my passcode\" messages may also move to cards by mistake.\n\n**5 → Dead weights.** The module also has a second unit, a penalty on account_security, set to weight 0. It has no effect.\n\nMistake: I used the Artifact publish action to edit `NOTES.md`, and it asked to upload the file. You did not approve it, so nothing was published, and I made the edit with Edit. Guard: I edit local files only with Edit or Write. This project has no lessons file. I suggest `.work/review/MISSES.md` for notes like this.\n\nNext step: if you prefer more PIN fixes over fewer unwanted changes, I can raise the bonus to 4. On my tuning sets that fixed 4 more PIN messages of 65 and changed 1 more non-PIN message of 140."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":456,"cache_read_input_tokens":191406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":456},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eec912b-7bc0-4263-9e21-2cd9f3856154","uuid":"d9635c63-5ac2-4773-85ee-118a70a838d3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T19:08:25.197Z","request_id":"req_011CgiQwiNLUnUjpvTyBzsvd"}
